mpv_kit licensing
=================

* packages/**, tools/**, example/**  — MIT (see LICENSE).

* native/mpv/**  — mpv 0.42.0 source plus the mpv_kit patches in
  native/patches/. mpv is GPLv2+; mpv_kit's own additions to mpv
  (render_vk.h is ISC like mpv's other public headers; libmpv_vk.c is
  LGPLv2.1+; the stream bridge is LGPLv2.1+).

* Binaries distributed by mpv_kit (v0.1.0-dev.10 and later) are built with
  -Dgpl=true and include GPL-only components: libcdio (GPL-3.0+),
  libdvdnav/libdvdread/libdvdcss (GPL-2.0+). The combined libmpv binary is
  therefore distributed under **GPL-3.0-or-later**. An application that
  ships this binary must be GPL-compatible and provide its own corresponding
  source. The Dart packages themselves remain MIT.

* The build scripts keep an LGPL flavor (`MPV_KIT_FLAVOR=lgpl`, which keeps
  -Dgpl=false and omits the GPL disc libraries) for self-builders. The
  release pipeline publishes only the GPL full flavor.

* LGPL/license-compatible components in the full bundle: FFmpeg 8.1.3
  (LGPL-2.1+), libbluray + libudfread (LGPL-2.1+), libaacs + libbdplus
  (LGPL-2.1+), libgcrypt + libgpg-error (LGPL-2.1+), libplacebo (LGPL-2.1+),
  libass and its text stack (ISC/BSD/MIT-style), and libcurl + nghttp2 +
  mbedTLS + libxml2 (curl license / MIT / Apache-2.0 / MIT).

* The Windows bundles additionally contain SPIRV-Cross (spirv-cross-c-shared)
  and shaderc (shaderc_shared), plus the SPIRV-Tools, SPIRV-Headers and
  glslang code linked into them. All are built from pinned source archives
  by native/build/deps.sh; they are licensed under Apache-2.0 (SPIRV-Cross,
  shaderc, SPIRV-Tools), an MIT-style license (SPIRV-Headers) or BSD/MIT-style
  licenses (glslang). Their license texts are shipped in the bundle under
  share/licenses/.

* Corresponding source: this repository (mpv vendor, patches, build scripts)
  plus the dependency URLs and sha256 pins in native/build/deps.sh. Release
  archives carry `sources-<tag>.tar.gz`; each bundle carries `SOURCE.txt`
  as the written offer. License texts are in `LICENSE.GPL`, `LICENSE.LGPL`
  and the bundle's `share/licenses/` directory.

* Legal note: libdvdcss (DVD CSS) and libaacs/libbdplus (AACS/BD+) are
  included at the project owner's request. Their distribution or use may be
  restricted in some jurisdictions; distributors are responsible for
  compliance. Users must supply their own AACS/BD+ key database.
